-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
What this licence covers (and what it does not)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The MIT grant above applies to the files in this packs/ folder written by the
Clear to Air authors: each pack's pack.json, its overlay pages
(overlay/*.html) and its skin.css. The shared overlay renderer in overlays/_shared/
that pack pages load at runtime is also MIT (see overlays/_shared/LICENSE), so a
pack stands entirely under MIT. The rest of Clear to Air (agent, control room,
relay, tools) is licensed under the GNU AGPL v3 or later (see LICENSE at the
repository root).

It does NOT grant any right to:

  * the name "Clear to Air", the lamp mark or the wordmark. These are
    trademarks and are not licensed under MIT or the AGPL. See TRADEMARKS.md.

  * game names, logos, map names, map art, character, hero, champion, agent
    and legend names, or any other artwork that appears in or is referenced
    by a pack file (including image URLs). These belong to their publishers
    and are used only to identify the game. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

  * team logos and player photos. The agent can cache these from Liquipedia
    into packs/<game>/assets/teams/ and packs/_players/ on the operator's own
    PC. They belong to the teams and the photographers; both folders are
    excluded from the repository.

  * fonts. The fonts the overlays use live in overlays/_shared/fonts/ and are
    licensed under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 by their own authors.
